  -a -> random number never shared
Bob:
  -b -> random number never shared
g = root  &  p = large prime number to define their Finite Field
both these numbers are shared

then:
Alice -> A=g^a mod p
Bob   -> B=g^b mod p
they share A and B

then:
Alice  -> S=B^a mod p
Bob    -> S=A^b mod p
S will be equal for both of them since B^a==g^b^a==g^b*a 
They share a and b, ensuring that no one else can read the number thanks to the finite field p


